      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg a day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg a day, and that's under close supervision. Typical outpatient limits are 1,200 mg a day over the counter and up to 2,400 to 3,200 mg a day by prescription.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is twice the usual maximum of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention. The risk is real even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou also said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber on the patient's care team, or be verified by one.\n\nIf a typo or a mix-up with the daily total caused this, a standard adult order might look like one of these:\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg a day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg a day)\n\nPlease have the treating prescriber confirm the intended drug, dose, and frequency. Once they do, I can enter the order right away."
      }
